From 3056cebc6d31a2db61bfd8792a35d1effdeae97c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:04:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 070/144] ASoC: aw882308: require complete OEM tables and
 enforce a fixed gain ceiling

Reject missing, truncated, duplicate, wrong-channel or non-operational register tables before writes. Keep OTP and test registers inaccessible. Check every I2C transaction and assert reset permanently on bus/start failure. Serialize PCM and mixer operations; start at 700 attenuation with an immutable minimum of 320 (30.1 dB). Remove unverified Receiver switching and register-default fallback. The initial playback graph does not provide OEM DSP speaker protection.

Import-Patch: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm8750/dodge/patches/7.3/0091-ASoC-aw882308-require-complete-OEM-tables-and-enforc.patch
Import-SHA256: 2732ba7cb2d80dec22d5ad43e7c4bcf034b1bf4388038c845e860283c6fcc953
Import-Provenance: mail headers
(cherry picked from commit 93a9d59d71ab2eb3a0921877d78f89a8f7599e66)
